    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1084">

                <pb facs="0807" n="731" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg731"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.512/1378</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Mr. Parker, representing
                        American interests</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-09-18T18:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 18, 1916, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>423. Department informed that recent Carranza decree requires repayment of taxes
                    paid Villa in territory controlled by Villa faction. Matter brought Department’s
                    attention by American citizens interested in property in State of Nuevo Leon.
                    Investigate and forward copy of decree if issued.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
